/-!
# Descent, Lemma 05VG: generation by global sections, site by site

Let `S` be a scheme and `𝓕` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module, and let `𝓕^a` be the
`𝒪`-module on a site associated to `𝓕` by Descent, Proposition 03DX.  Descent, Lemma 05VG asserts
that `𝓕` has a property of Modules on Sites, Definitions 03DE, 03DL and 03ER, if and only if `𝓕^a`
has it.  This file records the property *generated by global sections*, Modules on Sites,
Definition 03DE (3), at each of the ten sites of the lemma, one statement per site.  On both sides
the property is `SheafOfModules.IsGeneratedByGlobalSections`, the predicate registered under
03DE "generated by global sections": on the side of `S` it is read on the ringed site of opens of
`S` with its structure sheaf, on the other side on the ringed site of `𝓕^a`.

## Main results

The ten cells of the row, in namespace `AlgebraicGeometry`, each of the form
`𝓕` generated by global sections `↔` `𝓕^a` generated by global sections:

* big site `(Sch/S)_Zar`: `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule_zariski`;
* big site `(Sch/S)_étale`: `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule_etale`;
* big site `(Sch/S)_smooth`:
  `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule_smooth`;
* big site `(Sch/S)_syntomic`:
  `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule_syntomic`;
* big site `(Sch/S)_fppf`: `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule_fppf`;
* small site `S_Zar`: `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_smallZariskiAssociatedModule`;
* small site `S_étale`: `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_smallEtaleAssociatedModule`;
* small site `S_smooth`:
  `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_smooth`;
* small site `S_syntomic`:
  `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_syntomic`;
* small site `S_fppf`:
  `Cells05VG.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_smallFlatSiteAssociatedModule_fppf`.

## Implementation notes

The big sites `(Sch/S)_τ` are the five topologies on one chosen big fppf site, and the comparison
functor is `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModule` at the topology `τ`.  The small
sites `S_smooth`, `S_syntomic` and `S_fppf` are those of
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.associatedModule`; `S_Zar` and `S_étale` are those of
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.associatedModule` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`, built on a big Zariski and a big étale site
respectively.

Each cell specializes the comparison at the functor of 03DX on the quasi-coherent subcategory
(`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_baseAssociatedModule`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallFlatSite.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`) to one concrete
site.  At the small Zariski site the equivalence holds for every `𝒪_S`-module
(`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallZariski.isGeneratedByGlobalSections_iff_associatedModule`); the cell is
stated under the source's hypothesis of quasi-coherence.

## References

* [Stacks, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory

